\title{zudiff: Shortest Edit Scripts, Unified Diffs and Patches}
\description{
Computes the shortest edit script between two sequences (atomic vectors, raw vectors or the lines of two strings) and returns it as data, with Myers' algorithm (E. W. Myers (1986) \doi{10.1007/BF01840446}) or patience diff. Builds hunks with context, writes and parses unified diffs, and applies an edit script or a unified diff. Equality is that of match(), so missing values, signed zeros, encodings and factor labels compare as R users expect. The algorithms are written in the 'Goose' programming language (\url{https://github.com/aardappel/goose}) and compiled ahead of time to C, which the package bundles.
}
